title: SSH Client Connecting to RDP Port
status: experimental
description: Detects ssh.exe initiating a network connection to port 3389. Attackers use SSH reverse tunnels to expose internal RDP to an external server; observed in the Akira intrusion where ssh.exe bridged connections to the local RDP port.
references:
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/06/29/from-bing-search-to-ransomware-bumblebee-and-adaptixc2-deliver-akira-3/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/20
tags:
    - attack.lateral-movement
    - attack.command-and-control
    - attack.t1021.001
    - attack.t1090
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\ssh.exe'
        DestinationPort: 3389
        Initiated: 'true'
    condition: selection
fields:
    - Image
    - User
    - SourceIp
    - DestinationIp
    - DestinationPort
falsepositives:
    - Administrators deliberately tunneling RDP over SSH
level: high
